### 4. Ports are fixed or allocated with TOCTOU races

- Soak fixed listeners: `realtime-soak.harness.ts:31-32,205,218`
- Runtime fixed listeners: `runtime-routes.test.ts:88,90,104,106,112-196`
- Durable module-level allocation: `durable-main-restart.test.ts:24-25`
- Durable allocation releases the first port before requesting the second; both calls can return the same port.
- Module-level allocation lengthens the interval between probing and child bind.

Use held reservations, created inside the test/harness invocation:

```ts
interface PortReservation {
  readonly port: number;
  release(): Promise<void>;
}

async function reservePort(): Promise<PortReservation> {
  const server = createNetServer();
  await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {
    server.once("error", reject);
    server.listen(0, "127.0.0.1", resolve);
  });
  const address = server.address();
  if (address === null || typeof address === "string") {
    await new Promise<void>((resolve) => server.close(() => resolve()));
    throw new Error("ephemeral port missing");
  }

  let released = false;
  return {
    port: address.port,
    async release() {
      if (released) return;
      released = true;
      await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {
        server.close((error) => (error === undefined ? resolve() : reject(error)));
      });
    },
  };
}
```

Usage:

```ts
const privateReservation = await reservePort();
const projectionReservation = await reservePort();
const privateOrigin = `http://127.0.0.1:${privateReservation.port}`;
const projectionOrigin = `http://127.0.0.1:${projectionReservation.port}`;

await projectionReservation.release();
const projection = await start(/* environment using projectionReservation.port */);

await privateReservation.release();
const privateBackend = await start(/* environment using privateReservation.port */);
```

This guarantees distinct selected ports and keeps each reserved until immediately before its child bind. Always release both reservations in cleanup if startup fails.

